WEBVTT

00:01.040 --> 00:04.050
<i>Hi. The name's Eva,
or rather it was Eva.</i>

00:04.210 --> 00:06.880
<i>For the last 10 years, I've been
in this crummy boarding school</i>

00:07.050 --> 00:08.430
<i>without ever seeing my dad.</i>

00:08.880 --> 00:12.100
<i>On my fifteenth birthday,
I decided to pay him a visit.</i>

00:12.350 --> 00:14.970
<i>He's a race manager,
the best there is.</i>

00:15.270 --> 00:16.640
<i>It didn't really go as planned.</i>

00:17.180 --> 00:18.600
<i>He was so different and so cold.</i>

00:18.770 --> 00:21.480
<i>I just couldn't tell him
who I really was.</i>

00:22.110 --> 00:23.320
I'm Molly!

00:23.650 --> 00:25.690
<i>It went downhill from there.</i>

00:26.030 --> 00:27.030
<i>One thing is certain,</i>

00:27.280 --> 00:30.320
<i>my father
won't get rid of me this time.</i>

01:56.700 --> 01:59.120
OK. Everyone up.
We've landed.

02:02.540 --> 02:03.710
Who knows where.

02:24.850 --> 02:27.730
Uh, I'm sorry.
I guess I fell asleep.

02:27.900 --> 02:29.900
What on earth
are you doing here?

02:30.980 --> 02:32.240
<i>Well, I, um...</i>

02:35.360 --> 02:37.280
I mean, there's no problem.

02:37.780 --> 02:39.790
It's really OK.
I'm your dau-

02:39.950 --> 02:41.330
A problem, sir?

02:41.910 --> 02:43.000
Oh, her again, huh?

02:46.630 --> 02:49.000
I thought you could use
an extra mechanic, sir.

02:49.210 --> 02:51.130
Molly, have you lost your mind?

02:51.550 --> 02:53.970
I have the best mechanics
in the league.

02:54.380 --> 02:56.890
As far as I'm concerned,
young lady, you're just a surprise,

02:57.050 --> 02:59.550
and I hate surprises.
Have I made myself clear?

03:02.060 --> 03:03.390
You should have known better.

03:10.820 --> 03:12.690
Watch your step, little mouse.

03:13.030 --> 03:13.940
What was that?

03:14.110 --> 03:15.650
I think the ship has stopped.

03:28.000 --> 03:31.920
Gentlemen, beyond this door
lies the unknown.

03:32.800 --> 03:36.090
The qualifying trials
of the Great Race of Oban.

03:36.300 --> 03:40.010
It will be certainly
the biggest challenge of your lives.

03:40.260 --> 03:42.390
You will give nothing less
than your best.

03:42.560 --> 03:44.390
And watch your step.

03:44.560 --> 03:47.230
From now on you are
ambassadors of the Earth.

03:47.480 --> 03:49.650
And don't even think
I'm done with you, miss.

04:12.170 --> 04:13.840
Wow. Look at these aliens.

04:14.000 --> 04:16.380
I bet no one has seen
aliens like these before.

04:16.840 --> 04:19.180
Let 'em come.
We're ready for them.

04:19.340 --> 04:21.800
Remember, Jordan,
we're ambassadors.

04:26.980 --> 04:29.640
Well, I didn't expect
the Avatar in person,

04:29.810 --> 04:32.440
but at least they could have sent
a welcoming committee.

04:34.610 --> 04:37.780
Sir, I think the welcoming
committee has arrived.

04:42.240 --> 04:44.580
Oh, great... another surprise.

04:44.740 --> 04:47.580
Somehow I feel
this won't be the last one today.

04:48.120 --> 04:50.500
Welcome to Alwas, earthlings.

04:50.710 --> 04:53.790
You are the 96th
and last team to arrive.

04:53.960 --> 04:56.800
I dare say
we no longer expected you.

04:57.460 --> 04:59.050
Let me introduce myself.

04:59.260 --> 05:02.720
My name is Satis,
faithful servant of the Avatar.

05:03.760 --> 05:06.180
I will be your temporary guide.

05:06.350 --> 05:08.520
Follow me and I will take you
to your lodging.

05:09.640 --> 05:13.150
I've never seen a race ship
from Earth before... futile.

05:13.360 --> 05:14.650
Sorry to disappoint you,

05:14.860 --> 05:16.900
but this is our truck, buddy,
not a ship.

05:17.110 --> 05:18.740
Our ship is right behind me.

05:20.780 --> 05:23.200
I see, I see,
giant flying cushions...

05:23.620 --> 05:25.200
Really, very impressive.

05:36.090 --> 05:38.000
Ee-aw, giddy-UP!

05:43.800 --> 05:46.970
<i>You may not see me now, Dad,
but soon you will.</i>

05:47.140 --> 05:48.350
<i>That's a promise.</i>

05:53.100 --> 05:54.600
This is the pit area,

05:54.810 --> 05:57.820
where the 96 teams live
during the competition.

05:59.280 --> 06:02.570
And this is your home,
the Earth team pit.

06:09.080 --> 06:09.790
<i>Wow.</i>

06:12.460 --> 06:14.330
You still have a few minutes.

06:14.500 --> 06:16.880
Use them wisely
for you won't have much time

06:17.040 --> 06:20.260
to prepare for your first race
after the opening ceremony.

06:20.590 --> 06:21.630
Giddy-UP!

06:21.800 --> 06:23.510
Let's get to it then.

06:34.310 --> 06:36.650
OK, Jordan. I want you
to test the laser turret.

06:36.860 --> 06:37.730
Yes, sir.

06:39.320 --> 06:40.690
Can I help?

06:41.690 --> 06:42.650
I guess not.

06:58.630 --> 07:00.420
All right, Jordan.
That's enough.

07:00.590 --> 07:01.760
Now try the other side.

07:06.090 --> 07:06.930
All clear.

07:09.850 --> 07:10.720
It's a beaut!

07:13.730 --> 07:15.440
OK, Rick. You're on.

07:24.280 --> 07:25.900
Try the reactor,
one at a time.

07:30.280 --> 07:32.290
Set her down.
We have a leak.

07:41.290 --> 07:42.380
So, what's the verdict?

07:43.130 --> 07:45.170
Looks like we lost a liter
of engine liquid.

07:45.800 --> 07:48.970
It's not great, but there should be
enough left for one race.

07:49.680 --> 07:51.470
With the equipment
we brought,

07:51.640 --> 07:53.970
it would take us hours
to make the extra liquid.

07:55.520 --> 07:57.440
I saw a part shop
on our way here.

07:57.600 --> 07:59.400
They're sure to have some.

08:00.480 --> 08:02.320
It's a pretty common thing, isn't it?

08:11.910 --> 08:13.910
Hey, Don, you old fox,

08:14.120 --> 08:16.910
you brought along a secret
replacement pilot, didn't you?

08:17.540 --> 08:18.750
Yeah!

08:30.640 --> 08:31.890
Wow, that was close.

08:34.100 --> 08:37.020
You know perfectly well
how I feel about female pilots.

08:40.520 --> 08:41.980
Figures he would see that.

08:42.150 --> 08:43.440
Huh! Whatever.

08:49.820 --> 08:52.070
Still she has
a little something.

09:11.260 --> 09:14.180
I'm back! I got it!
I found some...

09:18.390 --> 09:21.100
Hey, what's the big idea,
you guys?

09:21.980 --> 09:23.020
Anybody there?

09:28.690 --> 09:29.530
Open up!

09:30.360 --> 09:32.240
If you think I'm just
going to hang out

09:32.410 --> 09:34.410
and wait for you guys,
you're dreaming.

09:43.710 --> 09:45.420
Wow, take a look at that.

09:45.630 --> 09:47.550
Is this uber-cool or what?

09:52.470 --> 09:53.430
Ouch.

09:53.590 --> 09:54.430
I'm sorry, I didn't...

09:54.890 --> 09:56.010
I hope you're not...

10:06.310 --> 10:07.860
Are you all right?

10:10.030 --> 10:12.070
Aren't you a bit young
to be running around

10:12.240 --> 10:13.990
without parental guidance?

10:15.700 --> 10:17.370
Do you really think
I was scared?

10:17.530 --> 10:20.120
You should see the teachers
at my boarding school.

10:20.290 --> 10:21.370
Now that's scary.

10:21.540 --> 10:23.410
Anyway, where are your parents?

10:23.710 --> 10:25.460
You're no older than I am.

10:25.630 --> 10:27.420
Well, in Earth years, perhaps.

10:27.590 --> 10:28.550
Prince.

10:29.210 --> 10:31.300
Prince Aikka, come here.

10:31.630 --> 10:32.840
Your dad's calling you.

10:33.590 --> 10:34.340
Uh, Prince?

10:35.890 --> 10:37.180
Please, forgive me.

10:39.930 --> 10:41.770
Hey you, stowaway girl!

10:42.180 --> 10:43.640
Over here!

10:44.230 --> 10:45.350
Here's the stuff.

10:45.520 --> 10:47.230
Thanks a lot.
It looks good.

10:51.400 --> 10:52.610
The name's <i>Ev...</i>

10:52.780 --> 10:55.030
It's Molly, got it, gunner boy?

11:02.540 --> 11:06.750
We declare the Races
of Alwas officially open!

11:38.570 --> 11:40.410
The Avatar.

11:40.990 --> 11:45.580
Proud pilots, the truce
of the Great Race of Oban

11:45.750 --> 11:50.250
has allowed you to prepare
for this day in peace.

11:50.670 --> 11:54.090
Your wait is now over.

11:54.590 --> 11:58.380
On Alwas,
you shall face one another,

11:58.550 --> 12:00.430
one-on-one,

12:00.600 --> 12:04.100
until only three remain.

12:05.980 --> 12:07.940
There is only one rule.

12:08.140 --> 12:11.150
You may achieve victory
by any means,

12:11.310 --> 12:17.110
as long as you do not attempt
to take the life of your opponent.

12:18.360 --> 12:23.530
Race like the wind, champions,
towards the great finals on Oban

12:23.700 --> 12:26.500
and towards
the Ultimate Prize.

12:48.230 --> 12:49.560
Yeah!

12:54.770 --> 12:56.530
For the first race,

12:56.730 --> 13:00.280
it's Nourasia versus Hortlum.

13:00.780 --> 13:02.530
We'll stay around for this one.

13:02.700 --> 13:04.580
Keep your eyes
and ears open, everyone.

13:04.740 --> 13:07.950
We need to learn all we can
about our future adversaries.

13:17.260 --> 13:19.630
-Hey, there's the prince!
-What do you mean, the prince?

13:20.300 --> 13:21.340
A Nourasian?

13:21.510 --> 13:23.890
I heard those lowlifes
are friends with the Crogs.

13:24.350 --> 13:26.180
I really hope
he flips his beetle.

13:31.600 --> 13:33.940
-I think he's kind of cute.
-What?

13:40.490 --> 13:43.530
Take a last look at Prince Charming.
He won't know what squashed him.

14:36.670 --> 14:38.040
Ew... That's gotta hurt.

14:49.890 --> 14:52.390
<i>Unsakafnourama katar.</i>

15:36.020 --> 15:37.400
Ha, great!

15:37.810 --> 15:38.650
You traitor.

15:39.400 --> 15:41.650
We'll have to watch out
for that one.

15:41.820 --> 15:43.320
He's a showboat.

15:43.530 --> 15:45.740
Anyway, I'm out there alone.

15:46.110 --> 15:48.490
You're not my chaperon anymore.

15:49.280 --> 15:50.410
Rick, wait.

15:56.040 --> 15:57.920
Fluid level,
back to 100 percent.

15:58.250 --> 15:58.880
Check.

15:59.040 --> 16:00.840
Can I help you
with anything else?

16:01.000 --> 16:02.880
Thanks, Molly,
but we'll take it from here.

16:03.380 --> 16:04.510
OK.

16:05.170 --> 16:06.340
I understand.

16:06.800 --> 16:09.220
You fired me
three years ago, Don.

16:10.050 --> 16:12.470
I know we've had
some bad times together, Rick.

16:13.060 --> 16:16.270
But I hope, well, I hope
we're past all that.

16:16.430 --> 16:19.020
Don't try to con me, Don.
I know you too well.

16:22.360 --> 16:23.940
What I'm trying to say is,

16:24.610 --> 16:26.190
I'm counting on you.

16:26.440 --> 16:28.780
We're all counting on you, Rick.

16:31.780 --> 16:33.620
You're just a surprise!

16:37.290 --> 16:38.540
Don't worry.

16:38.830 --> 16:40.500
I'll win your tin cup.

16:40.830 --> 16:42.420
Don't I always?

16:46.550 --> 16:49.300
Well, well, well,
what have we got here,

16:49.470 --> 16:51.340
a little eavesdropping mouse.

16:51.510 --> 16:52.720
No, I...

16:53.680 --> 16:55.140
Come on.
Don't make such a face.

16:57.640 --> 17:01.150
When I started, Don Wei
didn't want me around either.

17:01.810 --> 17:04.570
In time, you'll find your place.

17:05.690 --> 17:06.440
<i>I, Rick...</i>

17:06.940 --> 17:08.440
See you at the finish line.

17:08.690 --> 17:10.610
I'll be there, little mouse.

17:15.410 --> 17:19.540
And now, it's Grooor
versus Earth.

17:26.090 --> 17:27.760
All set, gunner boy?

17:27.920 --> 17:29.550
Ready. Just keep
your sunglasses on.

17:29.720 --> 17:31.970
He's got it coming.
He's going down in flames.

17:46.360 --> 17:47.570
Let's make it happen.

17:50.440 --> 17:53.570
It's a piece of junk, but it's made
of polarized titanium.

17:54.160 --> 17:55.320
Terrific, I guess.

17:55.490 --> 17:57.790
He means if you play
bumper cars with this guy,

17:57.950 --> 17:59.450
you're going home by email.

17:59.750 --> 18:01.830
I'll try to keep that in mind.

18:24.150 --> 18:26.020
Line me up,
I don't have a clear shot.

18:26.190 --> 18:27.190
He's all yours.

18:28.900 --> 18:30.690
Take that, you alien scum!

18:50.300 --> 18:51.300
What was that?

19:06.150 --> 19:07.650
<i>Something's not right.</i>

19:09.070 --> 19:12.320
Koji, remind me next time
to raise the laser power by 30 percent.

19:12.940 --> 19:14.030
Check.

19:14.900 --> 19:16.820
Molly, what are you doing here?

19:17.070 --> 19:18.660
Something's very wrong.

19:18.820 --> 19:20.530
I think something's
going to happen to Rick.

19:20.700 --> 19:22.410
I just know it.

19:23.540 --> 19:24.460
How's the body?

19:24.620 --> 19:27.500
The damage control:
OK, at 71 percent.

19:27.880 --> 19:28.830
Coming through.

19:36.880 --> 19:39.100
I think we got this guy beat.

19:39.300 --> 19:41.640
Molly, everything's just fine.

19:42.720 --> 19:45.060
Why don't you find
a nice spot somewhere outside

19:45.180 --> 19:46.520
and enjoy the show?

20:06.120 --> 20:08.210
Well, I guess I was
just imagining things.

20:11.420 --> 20:12.210
Go Rick! Come on!

20:13.750 --> 20:14.960
Surge of heat
in the cooling system!

20:15.670 --> 20:17.300
What? This is not good.

20:34.150 --> 20:35.650
Here they come, Daddy.

20:35.820 --> 20:38.570
-I can't see.
-OK, Eva. Time for a piggyback.

20:39.570 --> 20:41.320
There, is that better?

20:41.660 --> 20:44.580
Yes, I can see her.
She's winning, she's winning!

21:01.550 --> 21:03.850
-I'm OK, Don.
-Where's Rick?

21:04.810 --> 21:07.100
Rick! Rick!
Hang <i>on...</i>

21:07.730 --> 21:09.190
I know you'll make it.

21:09.350 --> 21:11.310
Very touching,

21:11.480 --> 21:13.860
but it's only
because you need me.

21:14.520 --> 21:15.900
Don't worry.

21:16.070 --> 21:19.150
I didn't come all this way
to blow it in the first race.

21:21.740 --> 21:22.990
Oh, Rick.
